<td id="S4.T1.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.46</span>76</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.8032</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.4423</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.1223</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">xsum</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">50%</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">11</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.46</span>01</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.8027</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.4304</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.1286</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">xsum</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">100%</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">6</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T1.2.7.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.45</span>74</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.7957</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.4275</td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.7.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.1284</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Metrics scores at the early-peak moment of the training history.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Direct inspection of the outputs allowed us to qualitatively understand the model’s behaviours during the first two phases: during the early-peaks, the models predicted either negated diagnoses (e.g., <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”No acute cardiopulmonary abnormality.”</span>) or empty strings. Then, during the forgetting-phase, the models produced either negated diagnoses or jibberish (e.g: <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”Arrested Arrested…”</span>, <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”Lake Lake…”</span>, <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”Nurse Nurse…”</span>). Unlike the smallest training size, both checkpoints manifested a third, new, stationary phase in the later training history, wherein the metric scores surpassed those during the early peak. This onset happened for <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">large</span>-50% at 106 epochs, <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">large</span>-100% at 48, <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">xsum</span>-50% at 65, <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">xsum</span>-100% at 32. In this phase, the models have finally acquired generalising abilities and were able to also generate diagnoses (e.g. <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”Small left pleural effusion.”</span>) on top of negated ones. We conjecture these three phases to be a manifestation of the more general phenomenon of the <span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">epoch-wise double-descent</span> behaviour in deep neural networks postulated in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 PEGASUS ‣ 4 Results ‣ Deep learning and abstractive summarisation for radiological reports: an empirical study for adapting the PEGASUS models’ family with scarce data." class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we noticed that the position of the early peaks w.r.t. epochs displayed inverse scaling with the train dataset size, leading us to assume that a generalisation ability could have been acquired for the smallest training sets, had they been continued for more than 530 (<span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">large</span>) and 330 epochs (<span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">xsum</span>).
Additionally, we believe that <span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">xsum</span> performed better than <span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">large</span> because the first checkpoint is better apt for the concise summaries <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> typically used in chest X-ray reports.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">As a complementary analysis, we rephrased the results of the checkpoints trained on 100% of the training data as a binary classification task of negated diagnoses and diagnoses introduced in <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Reference cohort ‣ 3 Methods ‣ Deep learning and abstractive summarisation for radiological reports: an empirical study for adapting the PEGASUS models’ family with scarce data." class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. Results are shown in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 PEGASUS ‣ 4 Results ‣ Deep learning and abstractive summarisation for radiological reports: an empirical study for adapting the PEGASUS models’ family with scarce data." class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and should be benchmarked against an always-negated diagnoses (dummy) classifier task, which, given the distribution of the two classes in the validation split, would have scored 0.62 precision and 1.0 recall.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr"></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r" colspan="3"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">large</span> 100 %</th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column" colspan="3"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">xsum</span> 100 %</th></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr"></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Epoch</th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Precision</th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r">Recall</th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Epoch</th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Precision</th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Recall</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">early peak</span></th>
<td id="S4.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">12</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.5579</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">0.6161</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">6</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.6242</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.3.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9384</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr">forgetting phase</th>
<td id="S4.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">30</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.3077</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r">0.019</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">23</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.5965</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.3223</td></tr>
